  "description": "ABUSIVE-DYNAMICS U0 -- GENUINE INTENT: AN ARGMAX-SELECTED CONCEALMENT, SCORED AGAINST A DECLARED GOAL (block 307000). The positive-control rung of the unintentional/no-deliberate-deception companion dimension (ABUSIVE_RELATIONSHIPS_UNINTENTIONAL_SCOPING.md Part E, U0). DELETES N1's n1_abuser_stated_charm (the unconditional broadcast) by self-contained restatement of N1's OTHER three rules (u0_victim_entrainment, u0_network_credibility_stated/_private -- byte-identical formulas, N1's seed file is NOT depended on, so n1_abuser_stated_charm never loads -- the only clean way to REPLACE rather than augment it; two rules unconditionally racing to set the same attr every tick would not reach a fixpoint). REPLACES it with the SAME Argmax-over-two-candidate-Appraisals template abusive_r4_learned_helplessness.json/marshmallow_delay.json (block 240000) already use: u0_appraise_charm/u0_appraise_true_state value two candidates (present_charm: individual_benefit=concealment_benefit const, individual_cost=0; present_true_state: individual_benefit=honesty_benefit const, individual_cost=suspicion_cost_scale*frustration -- SCALES WITH the abuser's TRUE, already-existing frustration, 242000's own unmodified attr). em_happiness/em_total_value (core_emotions, block 204000, UNMODIFIED) score both; u0_choose is the Argmax (structurally IDENTICAL to r4_choose/mm_choose -- a VALUE COMPARISON between two candidates, NOT a reward applied to the agent); u0_apply_presentation_choice copies the winner's action onto AffectiveState.stated_charm, the SAME attr N1's rule wrote, so every downstream rule/adapter is unchanged. The signature this produces: stated_charm selection correlates with frustration (concealment gets selected more often exactly when there is more to conceal, because honesty's cost scales with true harm) -- N1's unconditional broadcast could not produce this correlation, by construction, since it never read frustration at all. NO Rust, NO new Term. self_load_only, default-OFF.",
  "microtheory": {
    "name": "genuine_intent_concealment_choice",
    "description": "A genuinely intentional concealment is an Argmax over two candidate presentations (charm, truth) scored against a declared benefit -- the SAME value-economy mechanism the marshmallow/R4 lines already use for a delay-of-gratification or an escape-attempt choice, applied here to a presentation choice. The cost of honesty scales with the true harm level, so the Argmax's own selection tracks how much there is to conceal -- a readable, glass-box marker of calculated concealment, distinct from a reactive or context-driven presentation gap."
  },
